Package: metavidence
Type: Package
Title: No-Code Meta-Analysis 'Shiny' Application
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = c("Valbert", "Oliveira"), family = "Costa Filho",
                  email = "valbert@alu.ufc.br",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-2864-0966"))
Description: A 'shiny' application that guides researchers through
    meta-analysis in three steps: load the data, choose the parameters and
    review the results. Covers pairwise meta-analysis of binary and continuous
    outcomes, pre-calculated effect sizes, single-arm proportions and means,
    frequentist network meta-analysis and diagnostic test accuracy, producing
    forest plots, funnel plots, leave-one-out analyses, subgroup analyses,
    meta-regression and publication-ready exports. Pairwise and single-arm
    models use the methods implemented in 'meta' and 'metafor'; network
    meta-analysis follows Rucker (2012) <doi:10.1002/jrsm.1058> as implemented
    in 'netmeta'; diagnostic accuracy uses the bivariate model of Reitsma et
    al. (2005) <doi:10.1016/j.jclinepi.2005.02.022>, fitted as a bivariate
    binomial generalized linear mixed model (Chu and Cole (2006)
    <doi:10.1016/j.jclinepi.2006.06.011>) following the Cochrane Handbook for
    Systematic Reviews of Diagnostic Test Accuracy.
    The application runs locally and no data leaves the user's computer.
